         delta* = 0.0379 dex (canonical) / 0.0469 dex (alt).  Below delta* the class is excluded; above it, it is not.  SPARC's own quoted intrinsic RAR scatter is ~0.05-0.06 dex, so delta* sits INSIDE the observational tolerance, which is exactly why the question is decided by the RAR fit and not by a no-go theorem

